WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.360
In this video
I'll explain

2
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.960
how we help our customers
succeed

3
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.040
with AI clusters.

4
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.680
I'm Christian Wenzel
and I've been working

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.880
with AI for 15 years.

6
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.700
Back then in seminars with
mathematical algorithms,

7
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.600
at some point with
recommendation systems,

8
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.610
meaning what will the customer
most want to buy next,

9
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:23.120
and today, well, with
AI agents, or rather

10
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.420
with clusters of AI agents.

11
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.330
The recipe for successfully
introducing an AI cluster

12
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.220
at a customer

13
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:31.900
consists of several steps.

14
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.210
The first step is:

15
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.900
just start.

16
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.470
We usually take on
a small task,

17
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.840
for example bookkeeping
or a second brain,

18
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.370
to get a cluster running
and gain experience with it

19
00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.480
and to notice

20
00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.720
where it works and
where it doesn't.

21
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.710
Then a second
step comes in:

22
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.440
the ongoing
support of this cluster.

23
00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.470
For that we have a monthly
call with our customers

24
00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.300
and look at
what worked,

25
00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.500
what didn't,

26
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.530
which rules we need
to sharpen,

27
00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.980
which models we need
to update,

28
00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.560
maybe switch to
a different model,

29
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.680
and which project we might
want to tackle together

30
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.020
next.

31
00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.500
To be able to make this
decision every month,

32
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:16.550
the customers' clusters send
all their telemetry data

33
00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.640
regularly to our
own cluster

34
00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.860
at Venture Labs.

35
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.750
After a certain
time,

36
00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.020
the cluster will adapt
exactly to your company,

37
00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.460
the errors become fewer,

38
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.400
the results become
more and more precise

39
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.940
and the cluster takes over
more and more of your own

40
00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.180
tasks.

41
00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.440
And then there's even
the next step.

42
00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.740
Then the question is, if an
AI agent takes over everything behind

43
00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.140
your screen like that,

44
00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.950
couldn't we also adapt
the way

45
00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.600
you work together
with IT?

46
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.790
That leads to
you as an entrepreneur

47
00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.510
and your employees spending
much less time in front of the

48
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.480
screen

49
00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.780
and instead talking
a bit more to the phone.

50
00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.160
If that sounds
interesting to you,

51
00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.440
then just book a
15-minute

52
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.300
call with me and then
we can take a look

53
00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.980
at how AI can also
help your company.
